Dependency aliases rename something you bind so it fits better in the current file.

### Two packages called `render`

Suppose two packages both export a function named `render`. You cannot bind both as `render` because names must not collide.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    @blog render as render_blog
    @docs render as render_docs

    blog_html = render_blog()
    docs_html = render_docs()
]

### Namespace aliases

You can also rename a whole namespace.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    @core/math as math

    value = math.sin(1.0)
]

### File-local scope

A dependency alias is visible only in the file where it is written. It does not change the exported name in the source file, and it is not automatically re-exported.

### No shadowing

An alias cannot hide an existing name. If `render` is already declared in the file, `@other render` is an error. Pick a different local name instead.
